# Purpose: example SSH host entry for the VM created by guides/local-vm/Vagrantfile.
# Problem Solved: provide a short alias for connecting to the VM without repeating
# the host IP and user each time.
#
# How to use:
#   - Copy this block into ~/.ssh/config, or adapt it to your local SSH setup.
#   - After that, connect with: ssh vagrant
#
# Notes:
#   - Assumes the VM private IP is 192.168.56.10.
#   - Assumes the SSH key is ~/.ssh/id_rsa.
#   - Adjust IdentityFile if your Vagrant VM uses a different key.

Host vagrant
    HostName 192.168.56.10
    User vagrant
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_rsa
